    `Father, I close this week with the word that is most needed in the aftermath of the worst decision — the word that says You repay the locust years, that You restore the deserter, that You recommission the denier. I bring You what the locusts have eaten — the years, the opportunities, the relationships, the purity, the time — and I receive Your promise not as comfort but as covenant: I will repay. Let me be Peter this morning — not the Peter before the denial, but the Peter after the restoration. The one who has been asked three times and answered three times and received the commission that the unbroken version of himself could not yet carry. Take what was lost and repay. Take what was broken and restore. Take what was wasted and redeem it into something that no eye has yet seen. The second chance is not behind me. It is ahead. I receive it today.`
